Findings:

`S3WP3-L-1` — [arrival_head_seam.py:336](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops-s3wp3/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival_head_seam.py:336), **BLOCKING**

`canonical_location()` is only `Path.resolve()`. It handles relative paths, `..`, and ordinary symlinks, but does not establish filesystem-object identity. Case variants on a case-insensitive filesystem and distinct mount aliases can name the same store with different binding keys. After the store is replaced with another lineage, opening through the alternate spelling finds no binding and accepts the replacement as `FIRST_CONTACT`, bypassing `LineageReplaced`. The lineage-keyed journal cannot help because the replacement presents a previously unseen lineage.

