Trust-reset entries are replayable. `trust_reset()` appends without validating current epoch continuity or freshness, and `_epoch_of()` unconditionally selects the last reset line. Empirical reproduction:

```text
before replay K 8
after replay K 5 epoch ordinals [5]
```

Scenario: reset from 10 to 5, advance and journal through 8, then retry/replay the old reset entry. Effective K falls from 8 to 5. A store rolled back to 5 then opens as `UNCHANGED`, resurrecting the abandoned epoch boundary without a new operator decision.

